KNOWNBUG
assignment-to-non-constant-index2.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.p0\] always \(##1 main\.a\[\$past\(main\.i\) \+ 4\] == 17\): PROVED up to bound 2$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The RTL construction rewrites an assignment to an array element with
a non-constant index into a with-expression on the whole array, using
the Verilog index as is. The offset of the declared range is not
subtracted, as done when lowering reads, and hence the write and the
read of a[i + 4] disagree on the element.
